From cbf66ccd5c9b445afde336cefd209a25729f7242 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: verity sp1-tcdot lane <lane@verity.local>
Date: Thu, 24 Sep 2026 08:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] TC_DOT_BF16: operands as free witness values (no memory
 access)

The executor reads a TC_DOT_BF16 step's 8 operand words without a memory
access (mr_slice_unsafe on both executors, no page-prot check), and the event
carries them as ab_words. The chip drops the operand address, memory-read and
page-prot columns and the link from the decode to the read words. Each
operand limb stays fully determined by its range-checked BF16 decode
(x = 2^15 s + 2^7 ef + m), so a row proves D = C + A*B for the operands its
decode columns hold; only the accumulator goes through memory.

A proof therefore says the chained accumulator is reachable from some
sequence of finite BF16 operands, not from the words the guest holds in
memory. That is sound for a relation that is existential in the operands, and
not for one that authenticates them.

Cost/complexity artifacts regenerated (write_core_air_costs /
write_core_air_complexity).
